<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Investment — AI-led trading performance | NYUKD</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Investment is the first NYUKD rollout track, focused on AI-led trading, transparent strategy performance, risk controls, and a future live dashboard."
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="../assets/favicon.svg" />
    <link
      href="https://api.fontshare.com/v2/css?f[]=satoshi@400,500,700&f[]=cabinet-grotesk@500,700,800&f[]=jetbrains-mono@400,500&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/tokens.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/base.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/app.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="sr-only" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <div data-slot="header"></div>

    <main id="main">
      <section class="page-hero">
        <div class="container page-hero__inner">
          <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
            <a href="../index.html">NYUKD</a>
            <span class="sep">/</span>
            <span>Investment</span>
          </nav>
          <span class="eyebrow">Practice 01 · First focus</span>
          <h1 style="margin-top: var(--space-4)">
            Investment, led by <em style="color: var(--color-primary); font-style: normal;">AI trading</em> discipline.
          </h1>
          <p class="lede">
            Investment is the first rollout track. The scope is AI-led trading: strategy design,
            risk rules, execution discipline, and a dashboard that will show real performance
            once live trading begins.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="split-layout">
            <div>
              <img class="section-visual" src="../assets/thumb-investment.svg" alt="Abstract AI-led trading performance dashboard visual" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <span class="eyebrow">What starts first</span>
              <h2 style="margin-top: var(--space-3)">Start with transparent performance.</h2>
              <p>
                The first public output should make the strategy understandable before it asks
                for trust. The page will evolve into a dashboard that reports AI-led trading
                performance, drawdown, win rate, exposure, and rule changes with clear dates.
              </p>
              <div class="feature-list feature-list--compact">
                <div class="feature">
                  <h3>AI-led strategy logic</h3>
                  <p>Clear explanation of the signals, market universe, time horizon, and trade rules.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature">
                  <h3>Risk before return</h3>
                  <p>Position sizing, drawdown limits, stop rules, and human oversight defined before launch.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature">
                  <h3>Live performance dashboard</h3>
                  <p>Real results will be reported with timestamps, benchmark context, and transparent caveats.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" style="background: var(--color-surface-offset);">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="section-head">
            <div>
              <span class="eyebrow">Dashboard scope</span>
              <h2 style="margin-top: var(--space-3)">What the trading dashboard will show.</h2>
            </div>
            <p>
              The initial dashboard will be a performance surface, not a promise. It should help
              visitors understand how the AI-led strategy is behaving, where it is exposed, and
              whether it is following its own rules.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="kpi-strip" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); margin-top: var(--space-8);">
            <div class="kpi">
              <div class="kpi__value tabular">P/L</div>
              <div class="kpi__label">Real strategy performance</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi">
              <div class="kpi__value tabular">DD</div>
              <div class="kpi__label">Drawdown and risk limits</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi">
              <div class="kpi__value tabular">WR</div>
              <div class="kpi__label">Win rate and trade quality</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi">
              <div class="kpi__value tabular">LOG</div>
              <div class="kpi__label">Strategy changes and audit trail</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p style="margin-top: var(--space-5); color: var(--color-text-faint); font-size: var(--text-sm); max-width: 76ch;">
            This dashboard is planned as transparent performance reporting for NYUKD's own
            AI-led strategy work. It is not financial advice, a signal service, or a promise of
            future returns.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section--tight" id="launch">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="coming-soon coming-soon--live">
            <span class="ticker ticker--live"><span class="pulse-dot pulse-dot--live">●</span> Live beta — Phase 01 shipping</span>
            <h2>The dashboard is open. <em style="color: var(--color-primary); font-style: normal;">Sign in to use it.</em></h2>
            <p>
              Four quantitative strategies — Alpha, Beta, Gamma, Delta — running on paper
              accounts at Alpaca and eToro Demo. Performance, regime scoring, and a
              live stock picker are visible to everyone. Operator controls (start, stop,
              risk overrides) require an account.
            </p>
            <div class="invest-cta-grid">
              <a class="btn btn--primary invest-cta__primary"
                 href="#" data-invest-launch
                 target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                Sign in to InvestAI <span class="arrow">→</span>
              </a>
              <a class="btn btn--secondary invest-cta__secondary"
                 href="#" data-invest-signup
                 target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                Create a free account
              </a>
              <a class="btn btn--ghost invest-cta__demo"
                 href="#" data-invest-demo
                 target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                Browse the demo — no signup
              </a>
            </div>
            <ul class="invest-features">
              <li>
                <span class="invest-features__label">Public</span>
                <span class="invest-features__text">Performance dashboard · Stock Picker (first 5 minutes live) · Control Panel (read-only)</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="invest-features__label">Account</span>
                <span class="invest-features__text">7-day live Stock Picker trial · Notifications · Personal filters and watchlists</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="invest-features__label">Operator</span>
                <span class="invest-features__text">Start / stop bots · Override risk parameters · Run recalibration and auto-tune</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="invest-cta__fineprint">
              Paper trading only. Not investment advice. The dashboard reports the
              behaviour of NYUKD's own AI-led strategies — not personalised
              recommendations.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <script>
        // CTA wiring — read the single source-of-truth URL from partials.js
        // (set on window.NYUKD_INVEST_APP_URL). Update one constant when the
        // dashboard URL changes; every button here picks it up.
        (function () {
          var url = window.NYUKD_INVEST_APP_URL || 'http://127.0.0.1:8080/welcome';
          // Default lands on the product's /welcome page which shows the
          // sign-in modal. ?mode=signup pre-selects Create Account.
          document.querySelectorAll('[data-invest-launch]').forEach(function (a) { a.href = url; });
          document.querySelectorAll('[data-invest-signup]').forEach(function (a) { a.href = url + '?mode=signup'; });
          document.querySelectorAll('[data-invest-demo]').forEach(function (a) {
            // The demo path skips the landing and goes straight to the
            // Performance dashboard so visitors see real data instantly.
            a.href = url.replace('/welcome', '/performance');
          });
        })();
      </script>
    </main>

    <div data-slot="footer"></div>

    <script src="../js/partials.js"></script>
    <script>
      window.NYUKD.mount({ base: '../', current: 'investment' });
    </script>
    <script src="../js/app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
